Subject: windows.ui.xaml: x:Uid, theme colours, MinWidth/MaxWidth, boolean Visibility and Window.Activated

x:Uid: an element with x:Uid="Name" takes the localized values of its properties from the app's resources
(Resources/Name/Content, .../Text, Header, PlaceholderText, Title, Label, Description, Glyph, the ContentDialog
button texts, OnContent and OffContent), through ResourceManager, which chooses the language. Our ResourceManager
can't list a subtree, so these properties are looked up in turn.

generic.xaml has WinUI's theme colours (SystemAltHighColor ... SystemListMediumColor for Light and Dark, Windows
10's values), Windows' default accent colour and its shades, the system colours, and FlyoutThemeMinWidth/Height
and ScrollBarSize.

FrameworkElement MinWidth, MaxWidth, MinHeight and MaxHeight bound layout (measure and arrange; Min wins over
Max, as in WinUI) and can be set from markup; they were ignored.

Visibility takes a boolean (true Visible, false Collapsed) or a boxed Visibility from a binding or converter.

Window.Activated is raised: CodeActivated once Window.Activate has returned, then on WM_ACTIVATE changes, with
WindowActivatedEventArgs.

With these, Xbox Accessories' LandingPage has its title, its "Don't see your device?" text and its buttons'
labels, and its view model's visibility bindings apply.

